# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the linked ABC (3D spec §4.1), used by test_abc_adapter.
# ABC is never instrumented, but ASan's allocator still sees its mallocs. Only ABC's own functions
# are named here (a frame anchored at the start of its name): a leak of the adapter's or of
# Odin III's (odin3_*, adp_*) must never be suppressed.
leak:^Abc_
leak:^Gia_
leak:^Cmd_
leak:^Extra_
leak:^Mem_
# A formula ABC cannot parse leaves its parser stacks and the expressions on them behind:
# Mio_ParseFormula (map/mio/mioParse.c) returns NULL on an error without freeing pStackFn,
# pStackOp or the Vec_Int_t expressions it made (Exp_Var, Exp_And, Exp_Or, Exp_Not, ... in
# map/mio/exp.h, each called from it). The adapter calls it to refuse such a gate library
# (bridge.c, adp_formula_parses).
leak:^Mio_ParseFormula
# The same leak when ASan's unwinder stops in the inlined expression builder (ABC is built
# without frame pointers): Exp_And (map/mio/exp.h:138, also through Exp_Or at exp.h:152),
# called by Mio_ParseFormulaOper (mioParse.c:77, :79), whose results Mio_ParseFormula leaves on
# pStackFn when it returns NULL (mioParse.c:380).
leak:^Exp_And
